      "typedIntoContentEditableBody": true,
      "readback": "Welcome to the TinyMCE editor demo!\n\nMeet TinyMCE, the Internet's most battle-tested rich text editor with over 60 features including: Advanced formatting, Export to and from Word and PDF, Accessibility and spelling checkers, Mentions and comments, and an AI assistant.\n\nSutradhar MCP baseline test.﻿\n\n⭐️ Popular features (including paid subscription plugins)\nCollaborate with @Mentions, discuss using Comments and review changes using Suggested Edits and keep an audit trail with Revision history.\nPaste from MS Word and retain formatting. You can even import Word documents! \nPower your email editor with Merge tags and Inline CSS output.\nHit the highest standards with Spell Checker, Accessibility Checker, Advanced Typography and Link Checker.\n\n🖖 Get TinyMCE\nTinyMCE meets all your architecture requirements.\nCloud\tSign-up for free\tAlways up to date, easy to maintain\nSelf-hosted\tLet's talk\tWith enterprise level support\nOpen source\tDownload today\tAvailable under the GPLv2+ license\nWhy TinyMCE 👀\nOut-of-the-box features save dev time. From tables and spell checking to full collaboration and accessibility compliance, TinyMCE offers features you’d otherwise spend months building.\nBuilt to scale with you. TinyMCE powers applications with millions of users. Its performance, reliability, and architecture are built for scale, from early MVPs to global platforms.\nWorks where you build. Whether you're using React, Vue, Angular, or vanilla JavaScript—or embedding it in SaaS platforms or internal tools—TinyMCE integrates smoothly into your stack.\nNo one has been doing this longer. You benefit from 20+ years of stability, security, feature, accessibility, documentation improvements, and enterprise support services.\n\n❤️ Go build something today",
